{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>His breath departs</b> — it is that which dwells in the heart." "<b>He returns to his earth</b> — because the bones are in the pattern of dust and they are the foundation of the body. And the meaning of עשתונותיו is his thoughts, as in: perhaps he will take thought, like: Elohim will take thought for me."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 146, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:55.311121201Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}